# =============================================================================
# The Omar Files -- .gitignore (code repo)
# =============================================================================
# This repo is CODE ONLY. Your chat data lives in a separate "data directory"
# outside this folder (default: a sibling folder named `data/`, see
# Pipeline/omar_paths.py), so none of it can end up here by accident.
#
# The patterns below are a belt-and-braces safety net in case something
# chat-shaped ever lands in this folder anyway (an old install, a stray
# export, a copied identities file). The tracked-data check in CI and the
# optional pre-commit hook enforce the same list.
# =============================================================================

# --- Chat data (should never be in this folder at all) ----------------------
/Raw_Exports/
/Reports/
/Full_Archive.*
/data/
Pipeline/identities.json
Pipeline/config.json
Pipeline/normalized_exports/
Pipeline/logs/
Pipeline/Tools/chat_analyzer/_chart_cache/
Pipeline/Tools/arc_analyzer/data/

# --- Phone-backup / decryption artifacts -------------------------------------
# Never commit the database or any key material used to decrypt it.
# (The `msgstore_export.py` tool itself is code and IS tracked -- see the
# exception below, without which the `msgstore*` pattern would hide it.)
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
msgstore*
!msgstore_export.py
*.key
*.crypt*

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- OS / editor cruft ---------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
